D0 estimates (ADC).  VDD = VREF = 3.3 V, 12 bit: LSB = 0.8057 mV, full scale 4096 codes.  kT = 4.142e-21 J (300 K).

== 1. What the ADC sees (SIMULATED, amp/sim/a4a_summary.txt): amplifier output noise = input-referred 1.54-1.80 uV x 1000 gain
   input-referred 1.54 uV  ->  1.54 mV rms at the ADC input = 1.91 LSB rms
   input-referred 1.80 uV  ->  1.80 mV rms at the ADC input = 2.23 LSB rms
   => the amplifier noise (~1.9-2.2 LSB rms) already sets the ENOB; the ADC itself should add <= 0.5 LSB rms (RSS +3 % at 2.1 LSB: sqrt(2.1^2+0.5^2)=2.16)
   quantisation noise alone = LSB/sqrt(12) = 0.289 LSB rms

== 2. ADC error budget (ESTIMATE; allocation in LSB rms, input-referred, RSS target <= 0.5 LSB rms excluding the 0.29 LSB quantisation)
   kT/C of the sampling cap (C_s = 16.4 pF binary DAC)                                  0.020
   comparator input-referred noise (allocation, D1)                                     0.250
   comparator offset (removed by offset in code / not a noise; INL-neutral, allocation 2 LSB max) 0.000
   DAC mismatch (random DNL/INL, D2; allocation)                                        0.250
   VDD noise / ripple at the decision instants (allocation, D4)                         0.200
   sampling-switch distortion + charge injection (allocation, D2)                       0.150
   RSS of the allocations = 0.43 LSB rms (limit 0.5)

== 3. Cap DAC (ESTIMATE).  The PDK gives NO local MIM mismatch (mimcap_statistical = one global skew, agauss(0,0.025,3); no VCR term is active in cap_mim_2f0), so the unit-cap mismatch is an ASSUMPTION:
   ASSUMPTION  sigma(dC/C) = A_C/sqrt(area), A_C = 0.5 %*um  (typical MIM; confirm / sweep in D2 with a per-unit agauss model)
   unit 1.0x1.0 um: Cu = 2.94 fF, sigma_u = 0.50 %, MSB-carry DNL sigma = 0.32 LSB, total 4096 Cu = 12.1 pF, array area ~ 6554 um2 (x1.6 spacing/dummies)
   unit 1.2x1.2 um: Cu = 4.01 fF, sigma_u = 0.42 %, MSB-carry DNL sigma = 0.27 LSB, total 4096 Cu = 16.4 pF, array area ~ 9437 um2 (x1.6 spacing/dummies)
   unit 1.5x1.5 um: Cu = 5.91 fF, sigma_u = 0.33 %, MSB-carry DNL sigma = 0.21 LSB, total 4096 Cu = 24.2 pF, array area ~ 14746 um2 (x1.6 spacing/dummies)
   unit 2.0x2.0 um: Cu = 9.87 fF, sigma_u = 0.25 %, MSB-carry DNL sigma = 0.16 LSB, total 4096 Cu = 40.4 pF, array area ~ 26214 um2 (x1.6 spacing/dummies)
   => choose unit 1.2 x 1.2 um (Cu ~4.0 fF): sigma_u 0.42 %, DNL(MSB carry) sigma 0.27 LSB (3 sigma = 0.8 LSB), binary-weighted, C_total = 16.4 pF (+ ~1 pF parasitics = C_s ~ 17 pF), array ~ 9,400 um2
   split (6+6, bridge) needs 64x larger units for the same MSB-array accuracy (sigma(MSB carry) = 512 sigma_u LSB) -> same total C, more parasitic sensitivity: no gain, not chosen
   kT/C of 17 pF = 15.6 uV = 0.019 LSB: negligible.  Needed for kT/C <= 0.1 LSB would be only 638.1 fF.

== 4. Decision 19: one SAR + 16:1 analog mux vs 16 SARs (ESTIMATE)
   per-ADC area: DAC 9400 + comparator 2000 + SAR/control logic 3075 (25 flops x 75 + 80 gates x 15 um2, ESTIMATE) + switches/drivers 1500 = 15975 um2
   (a) 1 SAR + mux: 15975 + mux (16 TG pairs + decoder ~1360) = 17335 um2 = 0.017 mm2
   (b) 16 SARs   : 16 x 15975 = 255600 um2 = 0.256 mm2  (14.7x larger); needs its own conversion clock + 16 x 12-bit result storage for the SPI side (192 flops ~ 14400 um2 extra)
   DAC switching energy 232 pJ/conversion -> 14.8 uW at 64 kS/s aggregate (same for (a) and (b): conversions per second are equal); comparator+logic ~ 1.3 uW
   DAC switching energy 232 pJ/conversion -> 29.7 uW at 128 kS/s aggregate (same for (a) and (b): conversions per second are equal); comparator+logic ~ 2.7 uW
   DAC switching energy 232 pJ/conversion -> 59.4 uW at 256 kS/s aggregate (same for (a) and (b): conversions per second are equal); comparator+logic ~ 5.4 uW
   amplifiers for reference: 16 x 245 uW = 3.9 mW (A4a) -> ADC power is < 1 % either way; power does not discriminate, area does (15x).
   mux acquisition: amp follower Zout ~ 1/gm_f ~ 10 kOhm (A4a: gm_f 69 uS at 5 uA, so ~14 kOhm; 10 kOhm used) + TG Ron ~ 1.0 kOhm (ESTIMATE: 3.3 V TG, W/L 10/0.5, 1.15-2.15 V)
   tau = (R_out+Ron)*C_s = 187 ns; settle to 0.1 LSB after a 3.3 V step: t_acq >= 10.6 tau = 1.99 us; after a 1 V step: 9.4 tau = 1.76 us
   follower sink limit: it sinks only its bias (3.3-8.4 uA, A4a): slew into C_s = 0.3 V/us at 5 uA -> a 3.3 V downward step needs 11.22 us (adds to t_acq); source side is not limited
   crosstalk (mux memory): residual after t_acq = step * exp(-t_acq/tau); for t_acq = 3 us: 1.08e-07 of the step = 0.000 LSB for a 1 V step, 0.000 LSB for a 3.3 V step
   16 off TG leakage on the shared node (ESTIMATE, silicon-like 1 pA each at 85 C, model gives ~0): 16 pA x 8 us / 17 pF = 7.5 uV = 0.009 LSB

== 5. Frame timing (ADS7953-style: SCLK clocks the conversion) (ESTIMATE)
   frame = 16 SCLK cycles: CS falling = sample/hold instant; SCLK 1-12 = 12 bit trials MSB first; SCLK 1-16 shift out the PREVIOUS conversion [4-bit channel ID | 12-bit code] MSB first; CS rising = start of acquisition of the next mux channel
   per-conversion time = 16/f_SCLK + t_acq (CS high). Aggregate rate = 16 channels x per-channel rate.
   1x oversampling: 4 kS/s/ch, 64 kS/s aggregate: period 15.62 us; SCLK 2.048 MHz -> frame 7.81 us, t_acq = 7.81 us (OK, >= 3 us)
   1x oversampling: 4 kS/s/ch, 64 kS/s aggregate: period 15.62 us; SCLK 5.000 MHz -> frame 3.20 us, t_acq = 12.43 us (OK, >= 3 us)
   2x oversampling: 8 kS/s/ch, 128 kS/s aggregate: period 7.81 us; SCLK 2.048 MHz -> frame 7.81 us, t_acq = 0.00 us (IMPOSSIBLE)
   2x oversampling: 8 kS/s/ch, 128 kS/s aggregate: period 7.81 us; SCLK 5.000 MHz -> frame 3.20 us, t_acq = 4.61 us (OK, >= 3 us)
   4x oversampling: 16 kS/s/ch, 256 kS/s aggregate: period 3.91 us; SCLK 2.048 MHz -> frame 7.81 us, t_acq = -3.91 us (IMPOSSIBLE)
   4x oversampling: 16 kS/s/ch, 256 kS/s aggregate: period 3.91 us; SCLK 5.000 MHz -> frame 3.20 us, t_acq = 0.71 us (too short for the 17 pF input at 10 kOhm)
   SAR bit-trial: 100-200 ns per SCLK cycle at 5-2.5 MHz; MSB switch drives 8.2 pF: needs Ron <= 0.1 us/(9*8.2 pF) = 1355 Ohm... (9 tau to 0.5 LSB in half a cycle at 5 MHz): W/L ~ 5-10 (ESTIMATE); comparator decision < 20 ns
   VREF = VDD: MSB trial draws Q = 8.2 pF x 3.3 V = 27 pC from the local supply; on-chip decoupling cannot supply it at 0.1 LSB (needs 336 nF): rely on board decoupling + low-inductance bond wires; the DAC supply must settle to <0.1 LSB (0.08 mV) before each decision (RISK, D2/D4: ringing of L=2 nH + board C)
   rate of VDD droop error if VDD is NOT ratiometric to Vin: 0.62 LSB per mV at mid-scale (code x dVDD/VDD)

== 5b. ADC INPUT MODEL for A4b and what it asks of the amplifier output stage
   model (ESTIMATE): sampling cap C_s = 17 pF (16.4 pF binary DAC + ~0.6 pF parasitics) behind a transmission gate Ron = 1 kOhm; 16 mux inputs, off-channel load on each amp output ~ 20 fF;
   the cap is connected for t_acq, then disconnected (CS falling) and its charge is not returned to the amp.  C_s starts at the PREVIOUS channel voltage: step = V_new - V_prev.
   SIMULATED A4a follower (sim/a4a_op.log): sink current Id and 1/gm_f per corner; DOWNWARD step into C_s = slew C*dV/Id then RC settling n*tau, n = ln(dV/0.5 LSB), tau = (1/gm_f + Ron) C_s (class-A follower: upward steps are source-driven and fast):
